      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effect of charged versus neutral N- and C-termini on the stability of the collagen triple helix was examined. Thermal denaturation studies at different pH with collagen model peptides showed that an ammonium group at the N-terminus destabilizes the triple helix more than a carboxylate at the C-terminus. A neutral carboxylic acid stabilizes the triple helix more than an amido moiety at the C-terminus."},
